# member-ocean probe route-coverage manifest — consumed by
# scripts/check_member_ocean_probe_coverage.sh. Format: <path> <status>
# status: probed | pending | exempt (exempt requires a '# exempt: <why>' comment
# directly above it). Every route registered in backend/src/lib.rs's
# v1_routes() must be listed. Regenerate with:
#   scripts/check_member_ocean_probe_coverage.sh --seed
#
# probed  — a test in backend/tests/member_ocean_probe_pg.rs exercises this
#           exact path against the member-ocean adversarial fixture (member
#           A/B, org admin C, live and archived).
# pending — genuinely ocean/graph-resolving (reads or writes through
#           ReachabilityResolver on a caller-supplied or resolved graph_id),
#           but not yet given its own dedicated assertion in
#           member_ocean_probe_pg.rs. Each is already gated by the SAME
#           ReachabilityResolver predicate this suite proves correct on the
#           routes it DOES probe directly (member_ocean_promotion_pg.rs,
#           group_b_probe_pg.rs, and this file all exercise that shared
#           predicate) — "pending" records that this specific PATH has no
#           row of its own yet, not that the mechanism is unverified.
# exempt  — not ocean/graph-content-scoped at all.
# exempt: account roster read, no graph_id/ocean concept.
/account/members exempt
# exempt: account roster member CRUD, no graph_id.
/account/members/{user_id} exempt
/activity probed
/atoms/{atom_id} probed
